                <!-- The Problem: Code Understanding Challenges -->
                <ProjectSection Title="The Problem" Icon="fas fa-exclamation-triangle">
                    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-6">Developers and AI assistants struggle with unfamiliar codebases. Existing tools show directory structures ("where code lives") but fail to capture behavior ("how code works").</p>

                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
                        <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4 flex items-center">
                                <i class="fas fa-folder-tree mr-3"></i>Current Tool Limitations
                            </h3>
                            <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                                <li><strong>File-centric organization:</strong> Shows directory structure, not workflows</li>
                                <li><strong>Static documentation:</strong> Quickly outdated, missing system-level interactions</li>
                                <li><strong>Fragmented relationships:</strong> Only immediate connections visible</li>
                                <li><strong>Lost architectural context:</strong> No project philosophy or team culture captured</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4 flex items-center">
                                <i class="fas fa-robot mr-3"></i>AI Assistant Challenges
                            </h3>
                            <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300 text-sm">
                                <li><strong>Version Mismatch:</strong> Hallucinating APIs from wrong package versions</li>
                                <li><strong>New Package Blindness:</strong> No knowledge of recently released libraries</li>
                                <li><strong>Confabulation:</strong> Plausible but incorrect code generation</li>
                                <li><strong>Missing Architectural Context:</strong> Code that works but violates team patterns</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white/[.02] rounded-lg p-6 border border-line">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">Critical Impact</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-300">
                            AI assistants lack Architectural Context: they don't know if your team prefers composition over inheritance, whether you use dependency injection patterns, or which design principles guide your codebase. This leads to syntactically correct code that violates team culture and architectural philosophy, requiring extensive manual refactoring.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </ProjectSection>

                <!-- Proposed Solution: Hybrid C#/.NET Architecture -->
